%% Sequenzdiagramm Fehlerszenario - siehe docs/architecture.md, Abschnitt 6
%% "Fehlerszenarien", Unterabschnitt "Rechnungserstellung fehlgeschlagen".
%% Einziges Szenario OHNE Rollback von Zahlung/Lager: Zahlung und
%% Warehouse-Commit sind bereits abgeschlossen, bevor die Rechnung
%% wiederholt fehlschlaegt - die Bestellung bleibt bewusst haengen statt
%% zurueckgerollt zu werden (Aufgabenblatt 2.3). Zeigt zusaetzlich die
%% Retry-Orchestrierung durch die Shop-Saga (nicht durch invoice-service
%% selbst) und den Invoice-Circuit-Breaker (Bonusaufgabe 4.1).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as React/Client
    participant Shop as Shop-Service
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ
    participant Warehouse as Warehouse-Service
    participant Billing as Billing-Service
    participant Invoice as Invoice-Service
    participant Audit as Audit-Service

    Client->>Shop: POST /orders (payment.scenario=invoice_failed)
    Shop->>MQ: warehouse.reserve.requested
    Shop-->>Client: 202 Accepted (Order=PENDING)
    MQ-->>Warehouse: warehouse.reserve.requested
    Warehouse->>MQ: warehouse.reservation.succeeded
    MQ-->>Shop: warehouse.reservation.succeeded
    Shop->>MQ: billing.payment.requested
    MQ-->>Billing: billing.payment.requested
    Billing->>MQ: billing.payment.succeeded
    MQ-->>Shop: billing.payment.succeeded

    par Lager wird trotzdem final ausgebucht
        Shop->>MQ: warehouse.commit.requested
        MQ-->>Warehouse: warehouse.commit.requested
        Warehouse->>MQ: warehouse.commit.succeeded
        MQ-->>Shop: warehouse.commit.succeeded
        Shop->>Shop: warehouseCommitStatus=SUCCEEDED
    and Rechnung schlaegt wiederholt fehl
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.create.requested (attempt=1)
        MQ-->>Invoice: invoice.create.requested (attempt=1)
        Invoice->>Invoice: PDF-Rendering - Testszenario erzwingt Fehlschlag
        Invoice->>MQ: invoice.failed (attempt=1, reasonCode=INVOICE_RENDER_FAILED)
        MQ-->>Shop: invoice.failed (attempt=1)
        Shop->>Shop: Circuit Breaker record_failure() -> failureCount=1 (CLOSED)
        Shop->>Shop: Order=INVOICE_RETRY_PENDING
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.retry.scheduled (attempt=2)
        Note over Shop: Backoff 0.2s * attempt, dann automatischer Retry
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.create.requested (attempt=2)
        MQ-->>Invoice: invoice.create.requested (attempt=2)
        Invoice->>MQ: invoice.failed (attempt=2, reasonCode=INVOICE_RENDER_FAILED)
        MQ-->>Shop: invoice.failed (attempt=2)
        Shop->>Shop: Circuit Breaker record_failure() -> failureCount=2 (CLOSED)
        Shop->>Shop: Order=INVOICE_RETRY_PENDING
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.retry.scheduled (attempt=3)
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.create.requested (attempt=3)
        MQ-->>Invoice: invoice.create.requested (attempt=3)
        Invoice->>MQ: invoice.failed (attempt=3, reasonCode=INVOICE_RENDER_FAILED)
        MQ-->>Shop: invoice.failed (attempt=3)
        Shop->>Shop: Circuit Breaker record_failure() -> failureCount=3, State CLOSED-to-OPEN
        Shop->>MQ: invoice.circuit.state.changed (state=OPEN)
        Shop->>Shop: attempt=3 = max_retries -> kein weiterer Retry
        Shop->>Shop: Order=INVOICE_FAILED (endgueltig)
    end

    MQ-->>Audit: alle Events dieser Bestellung (Routing-Key "#")

    Note over Shop: Order bleibt dauerhaft INVOICE_FAILED - Zahlung und<br/>Warehouse-Commit werden NICHT zurueckgerollt (siehe Abschnitt 6.4).

    Note over Client,Shop: Client pollt zwischenzeitlich GET /orders/{orderId}
    Client->>Shop: GET /orders/{orderId}
    Shop-->>Client: 200 OK (status=INVOICE_FAILED)
